# Cloudflare Pages redirects. Order matters: first match wins.
#
# Until now the no-trailing-slash form of every article URL fell through to the
# platform default, which answers 307 Temporary Redirect. The destination was
# right, so nothing was broken, but 307 tells a crawler the move might be
# temporary, and every inbound link or share written without the slash keeps
# resolving through a temporary redirect. These rules pin it to 301.
#
# One line per real directory rather than a catch-all: a /* rule would also
# match the trailing-slash form and loop. Adding a page means adding its line.
#
# The canonical form stays the trailing-slash one. Every rule is an exact path
# match, so the order below does not change the outcome; it is grouped shallow to
# deep only so the file stays readable as pages are added.

